{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And for your livestock and for the wild beast.</b> If the wild beast eats — livestock, all the more so, for its food is upon you! What does Scripture mean by 'and for your livestock'? It draws an analogy from livestock to the wild beast: as long as the wild beast eats from the field, feed your livestock from the house; when the wild beast finishes from the field, finish off your livestock from the house."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:12.248712359Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}